  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - amqtt's client API is asyncio-based (coroutine connect()/publish()/disconnect()); the source code's synchronous, callback-style lifecycle (mqtt.Client() 
-> client.connect(host, port) -> client.publish(...) returning an object with .rc) has no synchronous counterpart in amqtt.
    - MqttSink.publish() is defined as a synchronous method returning an int (getattr(info, 'rc', 0)); amqtt.publish() returns a coroutine/awaitable, not an 
object with an .rc attribute, so the return-value semantics cannot be reproduced without making the entire call chain async.
    - There is no non-structural glue code that converts a fire-and-forget async coroutine library into the synchronous drop-in replacement the rest of the 
codebase (MqttSink, _default_client) is written against; achieving compatibility would require rewriting MqttSink and its callers to be async, which is outside
the scope of wrapper-only glue.
    - amqtt is noted as unmaintained/deprecated, raising additional risk for adopting it as the production MQTT client, independent of the async/sync 
structural mismatch.
